      "api_error_status": null,
      "result": "`more_itertools.chunked` keeps the leftover items and returns them as a shorter final chunk. It doesn't pad or drop them.\n\n```python\n>>> list(chunked([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7], 3))\n[[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6], [7]]\n```\n\nIf you want different behavior, there are two options:\n- `chunked(iterable, n, strict=True)` raises a `ValueError` if the last chunk would be short. Added in more-itertools 8.9.\n- `grouper(iterable, n, incomplete='fill', fillvalue=None)` pads the last group. It can also ignore the leftover items (`incomplete='ignore'`) or raise (`incomplete='strict'`).\n\nI'm answering from memory and didn't check the docs for the version you have installed.",
